","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":288956,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"festival","ranking":0.3968502629920499,"languages":{"spoken":["en","nl","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":118,"translations":{"de":"Festival","pt":null,"en":"Festival","it":"Festival","cn":null,"fr":"Festival","sp":"Festival","nl":"Festival"}},"others":{}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"pt":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"en":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":"PhotoBrussels Festival, the must-attend event for photography in Brussels is back for its 8th edition! The festival offers visitors a journey through exhibitions in various cultural venues throughout the Belgian capital. By not limiting itself to just one exhibition space, PhotoBrussels Festival allows visitors to discover different facets of Brussels while exploring photography. ","longdescr":"Created in 2016 at the initiative of Hangar by Delphine Dumont, PhotoBrussels Festival aims to bring together, for one month, all enthusiasts, stakeholders and professionals of contemporary photography. Since 2022, the establishment of the Photo Art and Culture nonprofit organization and the implementation of the coordination committee have strengthened the reputation and importance of the festival in Brussels.\n\nPhotoBrussels Festival is an event that establishes Brussels as an essential player in the international photographic scene and is part of the European Month of Photography (EMOP), a network of photography festivals present in various European cities such as Berlin, Lisbon, Luxembourg, Paris, Vienna and Brussels. PhotoBrussels Festival attracts a local audience (Brussels-Capital Region), Belgian, and international visitors (neighboring countries), as well as photography professionals, collectors and art gallery and cultural center enthusiasts.\n\nPhotoBrussels Festival is the essential photography event in Brussels.\nThe festival offers visitors an exhibition circuit in various cultural venues (art galleries, museums, art centers) within the Belgian capital.\n\nFind all the information on the website: https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/\n","performers":"Committee: Atelier Contraste, Box Galerie, Contretype, L'Enfant Sauvage, Fondation A Stichting, Hangar, La Nombreuse, Stieglitz19, Tipi Bookshop.\n\nAll the participating organisations can be found on our website: https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"it":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"cn":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"fr":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":"PhotoBrussels Festival, l'\u00e9v\u00e9nement incontournable de la photographie \u00e0 Bruxelles, est de retour pour sa 8e \u00e9dition ! Le festival propose aux visiteurs un voyage \u00e0 travers des expositions dans divers lieux culturels de la capitale. En ne se limitant pas \u00e0 un seul espace d'exposition, le festival permet aux visiteurs de d\u00e9couvrir diff\u00e9rentes facettes de Bruxelles tout en explorant la photographie. ","longdescr":"Cr\u00e9\u00e9 en 2016 \u00e0 l\u2019initiative du Hangar par Delphine Dumont, PhotoBrussels Festival a pour objectif de r\u00e9unir pendant un mois tous les amateurs, acteurs et professionnels de la photographie contemporaine. Depuis 2022, la cr\u00e9ation de l\u2019ASBL Photo Art et Culture et la mise en place du comit\u00e9 de coordination ont permis de renforcer la r\u00e9putation et l\u2019importance du festival \u00e0 Bruxelles.\n\nPhotoBrussels Festival est un \u00e9v\u00e9nement qui donne \u00e0 Bruxelles sa place d\u2019acteur incontournable de la sc\u00e8ne photographique internationale et s\u2019inscrit dans le cadre du Mois Europ\u00e9en de la Photographie (EMOP), un r\u00e9seau de festivals de photographie pr\u00e9sent dans diff\u00e9rentes villes europ\u00e9ennes telles que Berlin, Lisbonne, Luxembourg, Paris, Vienne et Bruxelles. Le PhotoBrussels Festival accueille un public local (R\u00e9gion Bruxelles-Capitale), belge et international (pays limitrophes), en plus des professionnels de la photographie, des collectionneurs et des publics amateurs de visites en galeries d\u2019art et centres culturels.\n\nPhotoBrussels Festival est le rendez-vous incontournable de la photographie \u00e0 Bruxelles.\nLe Festival propose aux visiteurs un parcours d\u2019expositions dans diverses structures culturelles (galeries d\u2019art, mus\u00e9es, centres d\u2019art\u2026) au sein de la capitale belge.\n\nRetrouvez toutes les infos sur le site : https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/\n","performers":"Comit\u00e9: Atelier Contraste, Box Galerie, Contretype, L'Enfant Sauvage, Fondation A Stichting, Hangar, La Nombreuse, Stieglitz19, Tipi Bookshop.\n\nToutes les structures participantes et les horaires d'ouverture de chacun des lieux sont \u00e0 retrouver sur le site : https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"sp":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"},"nl":{"name":"PhotoBrussels Festival","shortdescr":"PhotoBrussels Festival, h\u00e9t evenement voor fotografie in Brussel, is terug voor zijn 8e editie! Het festival biedt bezoekers een reis langs tentoonstellingen op verschillende culturele locaties in de Belgische hoofdstad. Door zich niet te beperken tot \u00e9\u00e9n tentoonstellingsruimte, laat PhotoBrussels Festival bezoekers verschillende facetten van Brussel ontdekken terwijl ze fotografie ontdekken. ","longdescr":"Gecre\u00eberd in 2016 op initiatief van Hangar door Delphine Dumont, heeft het PhotoBrussels Festival tot doel gedurende \u00e9\u00e9n maand alle liefhebbers, belanghebbenden en professionals op het gebied van hedendaagse fotografie samen te brengen. Sinds 2022 hebben de oprichting van de vzw Photo Art en Culture en de instelling van het co\u00f6rdinatiecomit\u00e9 de reputatie en het belang van het festival in Brussel versterkt.\n\nPhotoBrussels Festival is een evenement dat Brussel vestigt als een essenti\u00eble speler in het internationale fotografische landschap en maakt deel uit van de European Month of Photography (EMOP), een netwerk van fotografiefestivals aanwezig in verschillende Europese steden zoals Berlijn, Lissabon, Luxemburg, Parijs, Wenen en Brussel. PhotoBrussels Festival trekt een lokaal publiek (Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest), Belgische en internationale bezoekers (buurlanden), evenals professionals op het gebied van fotografie, verzamelaars en liefhebbers van kunstgalerijen en culturele centra.\n\nPhotoBrussels Festival is het essenti\u00eble fotografie-evenement in Brussel. Het festival\nbiedt bezoekers een tentoonstellingsparcours in verschillende culturele locaties (kunstgalerijen, musea, kunstcentra) binnen de Belgische hoofdstad.\n\nLees meer op de website: https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/\n","performers":"Commissie: Atelier Contraste, Box Galerie, Contretype, L'Enfant Sauvage, Stichting A, Hangar, La Nombreuse, Stieglitz19, Tipi Bookshop.\n\nAlle deelnemende organisaties zijn te vinden op onze website: https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.photobrusselsfestival.com\/","email":"info@photobrusselsfestival.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004439"}},"place":{"id":245448,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Divers lieux \u00e0 Bruxelles","address_street_name":null,"address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Divers lieux \u00e0 Bruxelles","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Divers lieux \u00e0 Bruxelles","address_street_name":null,"address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"websit