,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2024-02-18T01:02:52+01:00","published_at":"2023-10-02T12:02:04+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":286390,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"expo","ranking":0.3684031498640387,"languages":{"spoken":["en","nl","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibition","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Exposition","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/fr\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"pt":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/fr\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"en":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":"Everyone knows the name Porsche, however there are still many secrets to be discovered about the make.\n\nAutoworld, in collaboration with Porsche Belgium and the Stuttgart Museum, are presently gathering \"Unseen\" models, cars never before revealed to the general public. Stay tuned...\n\nCome and dream with Porsche, from 8th December 2023 until 23rd February 2024!","longdescr":"Porsche. Is there any other brand of car that makes people dream any harder? For 75 years Porsche has been building dream cars.\n\nFollowing up the exhibitions 'Porsche - Electric to Electric' in 2013 and 'Porsche 356 - 70 Years', Autoworld continues its successful cooperation with Porsche Belgium and the Porsche Museum in Stuttgart with a new and unprecedented collection of exclusive Porsches, thematically collected in a unique setting, taking you into Porsche's overwhelming dream world.\n\nIn the process, the storytelling goes far beyond just the wonderful cars.\n\nIn addition to the beautiful cars, the exhibition also focuses on the people behind the brand. People who, like Ferry Porsche, have never stopped believing in their dreams, achieving great things and bringing great ideas to life. The stories of international and Belgian personalities are highlighted in the various theme groups. Examples include Jacky Ickx, Johan Dirickx, Thierry Boutsen, Laurens Vanthoor, Andr\u00e9 Lotterer... \n\nReality often begins with a dream. Every Porsche with a concept.\n\nAutoworld collected 9 Porsche concept cars never before exhibited in Belgium and shows them next to the production model. From the 984 that would become the 914, untill the Taycan prototype dreaming of an alternative future, passing by the 989 (Panamera project), the 959 Group B study, the 911 Vision Safari... And many other models next to these. \n\nNaturally, the 911 forms a separate theme within the exposition  \"Porsche, Driven By Dreams\" with once again a unique collection covering the 8 generations of the illustrious Nine Eleven.\n\n\"Porsche, Driven By Dreams\" wants to show more than dream cars.\n\nThe renowned Belgian street artist Vexx, known for his Porsche Vision Gran Turismo that will be present untill January 8th 2024, will be on site exclusively on december 7th and 8th for Autoworld with a Porsche themed animation.\n\nAnother artist, renowned photographer Bart Kuykens, will exhibit his work, in which the Porsche 911 invariably plays a prominent role. \n\n75 years ago, Ferdinand Porsche made his absolute dream come true by building his own dream car.\n\nThat dream has since become history. From the very first 356 \"Gmund,\" built in a barn in the village of the same name in Austria, to other classics that have helped turn Ferdinand Porsche's dream into reality. \n\nOther brands can only dream of Porsche's success in motorsports. Porsche invariably gives its opponents a proverbial nightmare.\n\nThe 991 RSR, 991 GT1, 919 Hybrid and Formula E Gen 3 are just some of the racing cars on display that have made Porsche the most successful racing car brand.\n\nOf course, the Belgian input is not forgotten with racing cars driven by such legendary drivers as Jacky Ickx, Thierry Boutsen and Laurens Vanthoor. \n\nIt was Jacky Ickx who made Porsche dream about the famous Dakar Rally. A dream that once again came true with the Rothmans coloured 959, among others.\n\nPorsche honors the successful Dakar models with the recent 911 Dakar passing by the D'Ieteren coloured 911 GT3 rally and the 953 Dakar. Autoworld honors Porsche's successful Dakar past in a separate, gritty universe of the expo.\n\nYoung visitor's dreams are given free rein in the separate area set up for kids' workshops where they can build the Porsche of their dreams using Lego bricks.\n\nA life-size Lego-Porsche will be on display in order to inspire the young Ferdinand Porsches. And with the racing simulator the next Porsche Le Mans winner might be discovered. \n\nDuring the three-month expo \"Porsche, Driven By Dreams\" Autoworld's permanent collection remains on display. Of course, the 'Bagnole' restaurant will also remain open to the public, as will the museum shop with an extensive Porsche collection, ideal for the holidays.\n ","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/en\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"it":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/fr\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"cn":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/fr\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"fr":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":"Tout le monde conna\u00eet le nom Porsche, mais il reste encore bien des secrets \u00e0 d\u00e9couvrir sur la marque. \n\nAutoworld, en collaboration avec Porsche Belgium et avec le mus\u00e9e de Porsche \u00e0 Stuttgart, est en train de rassembler des \"Unseen\", des voitures jamais r\u00e9v\u00e9l\u00e9es au public jusque maintenant. Stay tuned...\n\nDu 8 d\u00e9cembre 2023 au 25 f\u00e9vrier 2024, venez r\u00eaver avec Porsche!","longdescr":"Porsche. Y a-t-il une autre marque de voiture qui fait autant r\u00eaver les gens ? Depuis 75 ans, Porsche construit des voitures de r\u00eave.\n\nApr\u00e8s les expositions 'Porsche - De l'\u00c9lectrique \u00e0 l'\u00c9lectrique' en 2013 et 'Porsche 70 ans\u2019 en 2018, Autoworld poursuit sa collaboration fructueuse avec Porsche Belgique et le Mus\u00e9e Porsche de Stuttgart en pr\u00e9sentant une collection in\u00e9dite de Porsche exclusives, pr\u00e9sent\u00e9es de mani\u00e8re th\u00e9matique dans un cadre unique, vous plongeant dans le monde du r\u00eave impressionnant de Porsche.\n\nMais l'histoire va bien au-del\u00e0 de simplement des voitures...\n\nOutre les belles cylindr\u00e9es, l'exposition met \u00e9galement l'accent sur les personnes qui se cachent derri\u00e8re la marque. Des personnes qui, comme Ferry Porsche, n'ont jamais cess\u00e9 de croire en leurs r\u00eaves, de r\u00e9aliser de grandes choses et de concr\u00e9tiser de grandes id\u00e9es. Les histoires de personnalit\u00e9s internationales et belges sont mises en lumi\u00e8re dans les diff\u00e9rents groupes th\u00e9matiques. Citons \u00e0 titre d'exemple : Jacky Ickx, Johan Dirickx, Thierry Boutsen, Laurens Vanthoor, Andr\u00e9 Lotterer\u2026\n\nLa r\u00e9alit\u00e9 commence souvent par un r\u00eave. Chaque Porsche d\u00e9bute par un concept. Autoworld a rassembl\u00e9 9 voitures conceptuelles de Porsche jamais expos\u00e9es en Belgique et les pr\u00e9sentera \u00e0 c\u00f4t\u00e9 du mod\u00e8le de production en s\u00e9rie correspondant.\n\nDe la 984 qui deviendra la 914 jusqu'au prototype du Taycan r\u00eavant d'un avenir alternatif, en passant par la 989 (le projet Panamera), l'\u00e9tude 959 Group B, la 911 Vision Safari... Et bien d'autres mod\u00e8les encore...\n\nLa 911, la quintessence de la voiture de r\u00eave c\u00e9l\u00e8bre ses 60 ans. Naturellement, la 911 forme un th\u00e8me \u00e0 part enti\u00e8re au sein de l'exposition \"Porsche, Driven by Dreams\", avec une collection unique couvrant les 8 g\u00e9n\u00e9rations de la c\u00e9l\u00e8bre Nine Eleven.\n\n\"Porsche, Driven by Dreams\" veut montrer plus que des voitures de r\u00eave.\n\nLe c\u00e9l\u00e8bre street artist belge, Vexx, connu pour sa Porsche Vision Gran Turismo qui sera expos\u00e9e jusqu'au 8 janvier 2024, sera exclusivement pr\u00e9sent pour Autoworld les 7 & 8 d\u00e9cembre avec une animation sur le th\u00e8me de Porsche.\n\nUn autre artiste, le photographe renomm\u00e9 Bart Kuykens, exposera son travail, dans lequel la Porsche 911 tient invariablement un r\u00f4le important\n\nIl y a 75 ans, Ferdinand Porsche a r\u00e9alis\u00e9 son r\u00eave absolu en construisant sa propre voiture de r\u00eave.\n\nDepuis lors, ce r\u00eave fait partie de l'histoire. De la toute premi\u00e8re 356 \"Gmund\", construite dans une grange du village du m\u00eame nom en Autriche, \u00e0 d'autres classiques, toutes ces voitures ont contribu\u00e9 \u00e0 concr\u00e9tiser le r\u00eave de Ferdinand Porsche.\n\nD'autres marques doivent se contenter de r\u00eaver du succ\u00e8s de Porsche en sport automobile! Porsche inflige invariablement des cauchemars \u00e0 ses concurrents.\n\nLa 991 RSR, la 991 GT1, la 919 Hybrid et la Formula E Gen 3 ne sont que quelques-unes des voitures de course expos\u00e9es qui ont fait de Porsche la marque de voiture de course la plus r\u00e9ussie.\n\nBien s\u00fbr, l'apport belge n'est pas en reste avec des v\u00e9hicules pilot\u00e9s par des l\u00e9gendes de la course comme Jacky Ickx, Thierry Boutsen et Laurens Vanthoor.\n\nC'est Jacky Ickx qui a fait r\u00eaver Porsche du c\u00e9l\u00e8bre Rallye Dakar. Un r\u00eave qui s'est \u00e0 nouveau r\u00e9alis\u00e9 avec la 959 aux couleurs Rothmans, entre autres.\n\nPorsche honore les mod\u00e8les du Dakar couronn\u00e9s de succ\u00e8s avec la r\u00e9cente 911 Dakar en passant par la 911 GT3 Rallye aux couleurs D'Ieteren et la 953 Dakar. Autoworld leur rend hommage dans un coin s\u00e9par\u00e9 de l'expo, un univers de sable\u2026\n\nLes r\u00eaves des plus jeunes visiteurs sont libres de s'\u00e9panouir dans la zone pr\u00e9vue pour les ateliers pour enfants, o\u00f9 ils pourront construire la Porsche de leur r\u00eave en utilisant des briques Lego.\n\nUne Porsche en Lego grandeur nature sera expos\u00e9e pour inspirer les 'jeunes Ferdinand Porsche' en herbe. Et avec le simulateur de course, le prochain vainqueur des 24 Heures du Mans Porsche pourrait \u00eatre d\u00e9couvert.\n\nPendant l'exposition de trois mois \"Porsche, Driven by Dreams\", la collection permanente d'Autoworld reste expos\u00e9e. Bien s\u00fbr, le restaurant 'Bagnole' sera ouvert au public, tout comme la boutique du mus\u00e9e avec une large collection de Porsche miniatures, id\u00e9al pour les f\u00eates de fin d'ann\u00e9e.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/fr\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"sp":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/fr\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"},"nl":{"name":"Porsche Driven by Dreams","shortdescr":"Iedereen kent de naam Porsche, maar er zijn nog veel geheimen over het merk te ontdekken.\n\nAutoworld is in samenwerking met Porsche Belgi\u00eb en het Stuttgart Museum bezig met het samenstellen van een selectie van  \"ongeziene\" auto's, die nog nooit eerder aan het publiek werden getoond. Meer nieuws volgt weldra... \n\nKom van 8 december 2023 tot 25 februari 2024 dromen met Porsche!","longdescr":"Porsche. Bestaat er een naam die meer laat dromen? Reeds 75 jaar bouwt Porsche droomwagens.\n\nNa de expo \u2018Porsche - Electric to Electric\u2019 in 2013 en \u2018Porsche 70 Years\u2019 in 2018 zet Autoworld z\u2019n succesvolle samenwerking met Porsche Belgi\u00eb en het Porsche Museum in Stuttgart verder. Met een nooit eerder geziene verzameling van exclusieve Porsches, thematisch verzameld in een unieke setting, word je meegenomen in de overweldigende droomwereld van Porsche.\n\nDaarbij gaat de storytelling veel verder dan enkel de wagens...\n\nNaast de prachtige auto's richt de tentoonstelling zich ook op de mensen achter het merk. Mensen die, net als Ferry Porsche, altijd in hun dromen zijn blijven geloven, grootse dingen hebben bereikt en grootse idee\u00ebn hebben verwezenlijkt. De verhalen van internationale en Belgische persoonlijkheden worden belicht in de verschillende themagroepen. Voorbeelden zijn Jacky Ickx, Johan Dirickx, Thierry Boutsen, Laurens Vanthoor, Andr\u00e9 Lotterer...\n\nWerkelijkheid begint vaak met een droom. Elke Porsche met een concept.\n\nAutoworld verzamelde 9 nooit eerder in Belgi\u00eb ge\u00ebxposeerde Porsche concept cars en toont die broederlijk naast het productiemodel.\n\nVan de 984 die de 914 zou worden tot het prototype van de Taycan die droomt van een alternatieve toekomst, via de 989 (het Panamera project), de 959 group B studie, de 911 Vision Safari en nog veel meer modellen. \n\nUiteraard vormt de 911 een apart thema binnen de expo \"Porsche, Driven By Dreams\" met andermaal een unieke verzameling die de 8 generaties Neunelfer omslaat.\n\n\"Porsche, Driven By Dreams\" wil meer zijn dan droomwagens.\n\nDe vermaarde Belgische street artist Vexx, bekend van de eveneens tijdelijk aanwezige Porsche Vision Gran Turismo die tot 8 januari 2024 te bezichtigen zal zijn, zal op 7 en 8 december exclusief voor Autoworld aanwezig zijn met een animatie rond Porsche.\n\nEen andere artiest, gerenommeerd fotograaf Bart Kuykens, zal z\u2019n werken exposeren, waarin de Porsche 911 steevast een prominente rol speelt.\n\nFerdinand Porsche liet 75 jaar geleden z\u2019n absolute droom in vervulling gaan door z\u2019n eigen droomwagen te bouwen.\n\nDie droom is intussen geschiedenis geworden. Van de allereerste 356 \u2018Gmund,\u2019 gebouwd in een schuur in het gelijknamige dorpje in Oostenrijk, tot andere klassiekers die mee Ferdinand Porsche\u2019s droom in werkelijkheid hebben omgezet.\n\nAndere merken kunnen slechts dromen van het succes van Porsche in de motorsport. Porsche bezorgt zijn tegenstanders steevast een spreekwoordelijke nachtmerrie.\n\nDe 991 RSR, 991 GT1, 919 Hybride en de Formule E Gen 3 zijn slechts enkele van de getoonde racewagens die van Porsche het meest succesvolle racewagenmerk hebben gemaakt.\n\nUiteraard wordt de Belgische inbreng niet vergeten met racewagens bestuurd door legendarische coureurs als Jacky Ickx, Thierry Boutsen en Laurens Vanthoor.\n\nHet was Jacky Ickx die Porsche van de befaamde Dakar-rally liet dromen. Een droom die andermaal werkelijkheid werd met onder meer de 959 met Rothmans-kleuren.\n\nPorsche eert de succesvolle Dakar-modellen met de recente 911 Dakar, de 911 GT3 Rally in D'Ieteren-kleuren en de 953 Dakar.\nAutoworld eert de Porsche\u2019s succesvolle Dakar-verleden in een apart, zanderige universum van de expo.\n\nDe jongste bezoekers kunnen in de aparte ruimte ingericht voor workshops volgen waar ze de Porsche van hun dromen kunnen bouwen.\n\nTer inspiratie staat er een levensgrote Porsche in Lego tentoon. En wie weet wordt de volgende Belgische Le Mans-winnaar met Porsche wel ontdekt op onze race simulator.\n\nTijdens de drie maand durende expo \"Porsche, Driven By Dreams\" blijft de permanente collectie van Autoworld te bewonderen. Ook het restaurant \u2018Bagnole\u2019 blijft uiteraard open voor het publiek, net als de museumshop met een uitgebreide Porsche collectie, ideaal voor de feestdagen.\n ","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/nl\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002810"}},"place":{"id":734,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld ist ein au\u00dfergew\u00f6hnlicher Ort, einzigartig in seiner Architektur, seiner Sammlung und den dort organisierten Ausstellungen.\r\nDas Museum befindet sich in einem repr\u00e4sentativen Geb\u00e4ude des Parc du Cinquantenaire, welches  1880 anl\u00e4sslich des 50. Jahrestages der Gr\u00fcndung des K\u00f6nigreichs Belgien erbaut wurde.\r\n\r\nMehr als 300 Fahrzeuge, Reisebusse und Motorr\u00e4der unterschiedlicher Herkunft zeichnen die Geschichte des Automobils nach und veranschaulichen die spektakul\u00e4re Entwicklung von Fahrzeugen \u00fcber mehr als ein Jahrhundert. Die emblematischsten Autos jeder Epoche erm\u00f6glichen es au\u00dferdem, die Entwicklung des Autodesigns von Anfang an bis heute zu verfolgen.\r\nThemenbereiche beleuchten spezifische Aspekte dieser Geschichte. Der \u201eSport & Wettbewerb\u201c Abschnitt zeichnet die Meilensteine des Motorsport (Rallyes und Rennen) seit 1906. \r\n\u201eMan darf nicht vergessen, dass unser Land im fr\u00fchen 20. Jahrhundert eines der wichtigsten Automobilhersteller war\u201c.\r\nIm neuen \"Media Room\" erz\u00e4hlen Filme, Videos und historische Dokumente diese Geschichte ebenso wie die automobile Entwicklung der letzten 30 Jahre.\r\n\r\nTempor\u00e4re Ausstellungen werden regelm\u00e4\u00dfig organisiert.\r\n\r\nWeitere Informationen und den Messekalender finden Sie unter: www.autoworld.be\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Esquecemo-nos frequentemente que o autom\u00f3vel foi um dos baluartes da ind\u00fastria belga antes da Segunda Guerra Mundial: Minerva, FN, Imperia, Nagant, Germain, Vivinus, para citar alguns dos mais importantes. A estrutura met\u00e1lica do museu foi concebida em 1880. Abrigou o Sal\u00e3o Autom\u00f3vel de 1902 a 1934. O museu pode ser considerado como um dos mais prestigiosos do seu g\u00e9nero na Europa, ou mesmo no mundo (cerca de 400 ve\u00edculos, todos operacionais). Podemos a\u00ed reviver a hist\u00f3ria do autom\u00f3vel, de 1886 aos anos 70, da Ford T, passando pela 2CV da Citro\u00ebn, a Carocha alem\u00e3, a Tatra checoslovaca e alguns modelos raros que pertenceram a celebridades do nosso s\u00e9culo (\u00e0 fam\u00edlia real belga ou um ve\u00edculo especialmente concebido de acordo com as exig\u00eancias do X\u00e1 da P\u00e9rsia, mas nunca fornecido).\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"An impressive historic building in Brussels, linked with automotive history, is home to Autoworld, the Belgian National Automobile Museum. Situated in the \u2018Parc du Cinquantenaire\u2019, the neo-classical building commemorated the 50th anniversary of the Kingdom of Belgium in 1880. From 1902 to 1936 it hosted motor\u00accar and motorbike exhibitions. Since 1986 it has treasured the major part of Ghislain Mahy\u2019s renowned classic car collection. \r\n\r\nOver 300 vehicles, ranging from cars and trucks to motorcycles, are on permanent display. From the earliest models of the dis\u00actant past to contemporary cars that prefigure the automobile of tomorrow, visitors are guided through the motorcar\u2019s history dating as far back as 1896. \r\n\r\nVarious cars representing the most exciting years of the auto\u00acmobile history since 1960 can be approached and admired from close by, thanks to a brilliantly designed scenography.\r\nSpecial sections focus on sports and competition, cars owned by the Belgian Royal Family, micro and bubble cars, and car design. The Belgium at Autoworld section is dedicated to the roots and history of the Belgian car industry. \r\n\r\nAutoworld is a museum on the move, with temporary exhibi\u00actions taking on various automotive themes organised through\u00acout the year. \r\n\r\nMore detailed information on autoworld.be\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/home","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld, la collezione d'auto pi\u00f9 prestigiosa al mondo, inaugurata nel 1986 \u00e8 ospitata nel sontuoso edificio del Palais Mondial di Bruxelles.\r\nAutoworld \u00e8 pi\u00f9 di unmuseo, vi scoprirete una collezione di pi\u00f9 di 250 auto che raccontano la storia dell'automobile  dalle sue origini. Una zona interamente allestitata con la scenografia delle gare di auto , un altra zona dove si racconta il la storia dell'automobile e del Belgio. Il tutto situato nel Parco  Halle Sud del Cinquantenario a Bruxelles.\r\nAutoworld, un museo vivente\r\nAutoworld \u00e8 un museo vivente dove vi attende la nuova sezione Sport & Comp\u00e9tition che traccia le grandi tappe della competizione automobilistica in una scenografia originale e dinamica. \r\nSenza dimenticare la sezione pedagogica che rappresenta in maniera interattiva e ludica i vari aspetti del settore automobilistico. \r\nIl museo propone delle esposizioni dedicate al mondo dell'automobile, ai personaggi chiave della sua storia e all'evoluzione della mobilit\u00e0. \r\n\r\nSe le auto da corsa vi appassionano non perdete il laboratorio di restauroche ha luogo ogni domenica.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld est un lieu exceptionnel et unique tant par son architecture que par la collection qu\u2019il abrite et les expositions qui y sont organis\u00e9es.\r\nLe mus\u00e9e est situ\u00e9 dans un prestigieux \u00e9difice du Parc du Cinquantenaire, construit en 1880 pour c\u00e9l\u00e9brer le 50\u00e8me anniversaire de la cr\u00e9ation du Royaume de Belgique. \r\n\r\nPlus de 300 v\u00e9hicules, carrosses et motos de diff\u00e9rentes origines retracent l\u2019histoire de l\u2019automobile et illustrent le d\u00e9veloppement spectaculaire des v\u00e9hicules sur plus d\u2019un si\u00e8cle. Les voitures les plus embl\u00e9matiques de chaque \u00e9poque permettent \u00e9galement de suivre l\u2019\u00e9volution du design automobile du d\u00e9but jusqu\u2019\u00e0 aujourd\u2019hui.  \r\nDes zones \u00e0 th\u00e8mes mettent en lumi\u00e8re des aspects sp\u00e9cifiques de cette histoire. La zone \u00ab Sport & Comp\u00e9tition \u00bb retrace les grandes \u00e9tapes de la comp\u00e9tition automobile (rallyes et courses) depuis 1906, et la zone \u00ab Belgium at Autoworld \u00bb rappelle que notre pays fut l\u2019un des principaux fabricants automobiles au d\u00e9but du 20\u00e8me si\u00e8cle. Dans la nouvelle \u00ab Media room \u00bb des films, vid\u00e9os et documents historiques relatent eux aussi cette histoire ainsi que l\u2019\u00e9volution automobile depuis les 30 derni\u00e8res ann\u00e9es.\r\nDes expositions temporaires sont r\u00e9guli\u00e8rement organis\u00e9es.\r\nPlus d\u2019infos et le calendrier des expositions sur : www.autoworld.be \r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/home","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"A menudo olvidamos que el autom\u00f3vil fue uno de los florones de la industria belga antes de la Segunda Guerra Mundial: Minerva, FN, Imperia, Nagant, Germanin y Vivinus, por citar solo los m\u00e1s importantes. La estructura met\u00e1lica fue dise\u00f1ada en 1880. Acogi\u00f3 el sal\u00f3n del autom\u00f3vil de 1902 a 1934. El museo puede ser considerado como uno de los m\u00e1s prestigiosos de su g\u00e9nero en Europa, incluso del mundo (aproximadamente 400 veh\u00edculos, todos en estado de funcionamiento). Podemos revivir la historia del autom\u00f3vil desde el a\u00f1o 1886 hasta los a\u00f1os 70, desde el Ford T hasta llegar al Citro\u00ebn 2CV, el Volkswagen Escarabajo, el Tatra checo y algunos modelos raros que han pertenecido a celebridades de nuestro siglo (a la familia real belga o tambi\u00e9n un veh\u00edculo especialmente dise\u00f1ado seg\u00fan las exigencias del Sha de Persia, pero jam\u00e1s entregado)","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Jubelpark","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Jubelpark, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld, het nationale automuseum, is gelegen in het hart van Brussel, ondergebracht in een prestigieus gebouw in het Jubelpark. \r\n\r\nMeer dan 300 voertuigen (auto's, vrachtwagens en motorfietsen) worden er permanent tentoongesteld.  De bezoeker wordt er langs de fabelachtige geschiedenis van de auto van 1896 tot nu geleid, vanaf de oudste modellen uit een ver verleden tot hedendaagse auto's die ons een blik gunnen op  de voertuigen van morgen en zelfs van later. \r\nDe collectie werd onlangs aangevuld met een groot aantal voertuigen uit de spannendste jaren van de autogeschiedenis sinds 1960. In een licht en luchtig decor kan het publiek de tentoongestelde auto's van dichtbij bewonderen. \r\nHier en daar werden themazones ingericht, waar voertuigen van de openbare diensten, auto's die ooit aan de Koninklijke Familie toebehoorden, microcars en modellen onder het thema Design Story en Sport & Competition worden tentoongesteld.\r\nCentraal in het museum bevindt zich 'Belgium at Autoworld', een ruimte die volledig aan de bakermat en de geschiedenis van de Belgische auto-industrie tot op de dag van vandaag gewijd is. \r\nIn de 'Sport & Competition'-zone wordt een overzicht gegeven van de grote perioden in de geschiedenis van de autosport (rally en circuit) sinds 1906. \r\nAutoworld is een museum dat voortdurend evolueert. Het hele jaar door worden er tijdelijke tentoonstellingen georganiseerd over verschillende thema's die verband houden met de auto.\r\nMeer informatie over de kalender van de tentoonstellingen vindt u op www.autoworld.be \r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"de":["Europ\u00e4isches Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["European Quarter"],"it":["Quartiere europeo"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"sp":["Barrio Europeo"],"nl":["Europese wijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"de":["Osten"],"pt":[null],"en":["East"],"it":["Est"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Est"],"sp":["Este"],"nl":["Oost"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":147,"location":{"lat":50.83992036,"lon":4.39340998},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2023-11-10T09:31:48+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:18+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":false,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":734,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld ist ein au\u00dfergew\u00f6hnlicher Ort, einzigartig in seiner Architektur, seiner Sammlung und den dort organisierten Ausstellungen.\r\nDas Museum befindet sich in einem repr\u00e4sentativen Geb\u00e4ude des Parc du Cinquantenaire, welches  1880 anl\u00e4sslich des 50. Jahrestages der Gr\u00fcndung des K\u00f6nigreichs Belgien erbaut wurde.\r\n\r\nMehr als 300 Fahrzeuge, Reisebusse und Motorr\u00e4der unterschiedlicher Herkunft zeichnen die Geschichte des Automobils nach und veranschaulichen die spektakul\u00e4re Entwicklung von Fahrzeugen \u00fcber mehr als ein Jahrhundert. Die emblematischsten Autos jeder Epoche erm\u00f6glichen es au\u00dferdem, die Entwicklung des Autodesigns von Anfang an bis heute zu verfolgen.\r\nThemenbereiche beleuchten spezifische Aspekte dieser Geschichte. Der \u201eSport & Wettbewerb\u201c Abschnitt zeichnet die Meilensteine des Motorsport (Rallyes und Rennen) seit 1906. \r\n\u201eMan darf nicht vergessen, dass unser Land im fr\u00fchen 20. Jahrhundert eines der wichtigsten Automobilhersteller war\u201c.\r\nIm neuen \"Media Room\" erz\u00e4hlen Filme, Videos und historische Dokumente diese Geschichte ebenso wie die automobile Entwicklung der letzten 30 Jahre.\r\n\r\nTempor\u00e4re Ausstellungen werden regelm\u00e4\u00dfig organisiert.\r\n\r\nWeitere Informationen und den Messekalender finden Sie unter: www.autoworld.be\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Esquecemo-nos frequentemente que o autom\u00f3vel foi um dos baluartes da ind\u00fastria belga antes da Segunda Guerra Mundial: Minerva, FN, Imperia, Nagant, Germain, Vivinus, para citar alguns dos mais importantes. A estrutura met\u00e1lica do museu foi concebida em 1880. Abrigou o Sal\u00e3o Autom\u00f3vel de 1902 a 1934. O museu pode ser considerado como um dos mais prestigiosos do seu g\u00e9nero na Europa, ou mesmo no mundo (cerca de 400 ve\u00edculos, todos operacionais). Podemos a\u00ed reviver a hist\u00f3ria do autom\u00f3vel, de 1886 aos anos 70, da Ford T, passando pela 2CV da Citro\u00ebn, a Carocha alem\u00e3, a Tatra checoslovaca e alguns modelos raros que pertenceram a celebridades do nosso s\u00e9culo (\u00e0 fam\u00edlia real belga ou um ve\u00edculo especialmente concebido de acordo com as exig\u00eancias do X\u00e1 da P\u00e9rsia, mas nunca fornecido).\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"An impressive historic building in Brussels, linked with automotive history, is home to Autoworld, the Belgian National Automobile Museum. Situated in the \u2018Parc du Cinquantenaire\u2019, the neo-classical building commemorated the 50th anniversary of the Kingdom of Belgium in 1880. From 1902 to 1936 it hosted motor\u00accar and motorbike exhibitions. Since 1986 it has treasured the major part of Ghislain Mahy\u2019s renowned classic car collection. \r\n\r\nOver 300 vehicles, ranging from cars and trucks to motorcycles, are on permanent display. From the earliest models of the dis\u00actant past to contemporary cars that prefigure the automobile of tomorrow, visitors are guided through the motorcar\u2019s history dating as far back as 1896. \r\n\r\nVarious cars representing the most exciting years of the auto\u00acmobile history since 1960 can be approached and admired from close by, thanks to a brilliantly designed scenography.\r\nSpecial sections focus on sports and competition, cars owned by the Belgian Royal Family, micro and bubble cars, and car design. The Belgium at Autoworld section is dedicated to the roots and history of the Belgian car industry. \r\n\r\nAutoworld is a museum on the move, with temporary exhibi\u00actions taking on various automotive themes organised through\u00acout the year. \r\n\r\nMore detailed information on autoworld.be\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be\/home","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld, la collezione d'auto pi\u00f9 prestigiosa al mondo, inaugurata nel 1986 \u00e8 ospitata nel sontuoso edificio del Palais Mondial di Bruxelles.\r\nAutoworld \u00e8 pi\u00f9 di unmuseo, vi scoprirete una collezione di pi\u00f9 di 250 auto che raccontano la storia dell'automobile  dalle sue origini. Una zona interamente allestitata con la scenografia delle gare di auto , un altra zona dove si racconta il la storia dell'automobile e del Belgio. Il tutto situato nel Parco  Halle Sud del Cinquantenario a Bruxelles.\r\nAutoworld, un museo vivente\r\nAutoworld \u00e8 un museo vivente dove vi attende la nuova sezione Sport & Comp\u00e9tition che traccia le grandi tappe della competizione automobilistica in una scenografia originale e dinamica. \r\nSenza dimenticare la sezione pedagogica che rappresenta in maniera interattiva e ludica i vari aspetti del settore automobilistico. \r\nIl museo propone delle esposizioni dedicate al mondo dell'automobile, ai personaggi chiave della sua storia e all'evoluzione della mobilit\u00e0. \r\n\r\nSe le auto da corsa vi appassionano non perdete il laboratorio di restauroche ha luogo ogni domenica.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Autoworld","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autoworld.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autoworld.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 736 41 65","phone_booking":"+32 2 736 41 65","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire, 11","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Autoworld est un lieu exceptionnel et unique tant par son architecture que par la collection qu\u2019il abrite et les expositions qui y sont organis\u00e9es.\r\nLe mus\u00e9e est situ\u00e9 dans un prestigieux \u00e9difice du Parc du Cinquantenaire, construit en 1880 pour c\u00e9l\u00e9brer le 50\u00e8me anniversaire de la cr\u00e9ation du Royaume de Belgique. \r\n\r\nPlus de 300 v\u00e9hicules, carrosses et motos de diff\u00e9rentes origines retracent l\u2019histoire de l\u2019automobile et illustrent le d\u00e9veloppement spectaculaire des v\u00e9hicules sur plus d\u2019un si\u00e8cle. Les voitures les plus embl\u00e9matiques de chaque \u00e9poque permettent \u00e9galement de suivre l\u2019\u00e9volution du design automobile du d\u00e9but jusqu\u2019\u00e0 aujourd\u2019hui.  \r\nDes zones \u00e0 th\u00e8mes mettent en lumi\u00e8re des aspects sp\u00e9cifiques de cette histoire. La zone \u00ab Sport & Comp\u00e9tition \u00bb retrace les grandes \u00e9tapes de la comp\u00e9tition automobile (rallyes et courses) depuis 1906, et la zone \u00ab Belgium at Autoworld \u00bb rappelle que notre pays fut l\u2019un des principaux fabricants automobiles au d\u00e9but du 20\u00e8me si\u00e8cle. Dans la nouvelle \u00ab Media room \u00bb des films, vid\u00e9os et documents historiques relatent eux aussi cette histoire ainsi que l\u2019\u00e9volution automobile depuis les 30 derni\u00e8res ann\u00e9es.\r\nDes expositions temporaires sont r\u00e9guli\u00e8rement organis\u00e9es.\r\nPlus d\u2019infos et le calendrier des expositions sur : www.autoworld.be \r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_v