nstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[48,36],"translations":{"de":["Architektur","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Architecture ","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Architettura","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Architecture","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Arquitectura","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Architectuur","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"POWER SAVE THE DATE","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"pt":{"name":"POWER SAVE THE DATE","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"en":{"name":"POWER","shortdescr":"POWER connects questions of energy and politics. The exhibition and accompanying program challenges viewers to consider how contemporary infrastructure relates to everyday life across intersecting concerns, including political institutions, citizen participation, geopolitics, energy transition, and climate justice.","longdescr":"POWER connects questions of energy and politics. The exhibition and accompanying program challenges viewers to consider how contemporary infrastructure relates to everyday life across intersecting concerns, including political institutions, citizen participation, geopolitics, energy transition, and climate justice. From oil and gas pipelines to domestic radiators, from wind turbines to recycling hubs, infrastructure is central to today\u2019s debates surrounding systemic change. Objects of intense political, social, and economic contestation, these infrastructures distribute power in both senses of the word POWER : as energy and as politics.\n\nToday, architects, landscape designers, artists, and urban practitioners perpetuate the regime of carbon modernity. Yet they are also in a unique position to shift discourse and practice toward large-scale energetic transformation.\n\nPOWER is an exhibition that brings together historic references, contemporary practices, and speculations on the future. The contributors are comprised of a transdisciplinary field of architects, landscape designers, artists, philosophers, historians, scientists, legislators, and nongovernmental organizations:\n\nMonira Al Qadiri, Rachel Armstrong, Sammy Baloji \/ Jean Katambayi \/ Daddy Tshikaya (On-Trade-Off), BAUKUNST, BC Architects \/ Babinigeysen \/ Schenk Hattori, Bernd and Hilla Becher, Oana Bogdan and Antoine Crahay, Constantin Brodzki, City Mine(d), Paul Duvigneaud, Feddes Olthof, Buckminster Fuller, Bruno Latour, Armin Linke, Andr\u00e9 and Jean Polak, Ren\u00e9 P\u00e9ch\u00e8re, Cedric Price, OMA\/AMO, Philippe Rahm, S+ \/ Arno Brandlhuber \/ Fosbury Architects, Fran\u00e7ois and Luc Schuiten, Karl Schwanzer, Bas Smets, Territorial Agency, The New Open \/ TU Delft, Willy Van Der Meeren, and Liam Young.\n\nIn parallel to the exhibition, the project includes POWER Talks, a public program of lectures, roundtable discussions, and film screenings which among others features Thomas Auer, Daniel Barber, BC Architects, Oana Bogdan, Arno Brandlhuber, Koenraad Danneels, Andr\u00e9s Jaque, Jeanette Kuo, Charlotte Malterre-Barthes, Philippe Rahm, Bas Smets, Paulo Tavares, Ola Uduku and many more.\n\nIntergenerational workshops will also be held as part of the POWER exhibition, in collaboration with BC, V+, City Mine(d), Bento, Auranne Leray, Louise Lainiez and many more","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"it":{"name":"POWER SAVE THE DATE","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"cn":{"name":"POWER SAVE THE DATE","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"fr":{"name":"POWER","shortdescr":"POWER relie les questions de l'\u00e9nergie et de la politique. L'exposition et le programme qui l'accompagne incitent \u00e0 r\u00e9fl\u00e9chir \u00e0 la mani\u00e8re dont les infrastructures contemporaines sont li\u00e9es \u00e0 la vie quotidienne. Ceci \u00e0 travers plusieurs th\u00e9matiques qui se rejoignent : les institutions politiques, la participation citoyenne, la g\u00e9opolitique, la transition \u00e9nerg\u00e9tique et la justice climatique.","longdescr":"POWER relie les questions de l'\u00e9nergie et de la politique. L'exposition et le programme qui l'accompagne incitent \u00e0 r\u00e9fl\u00e9chir \u00e0 la mani\u00e8re dont les infrastructures contemporaines sont li\u00e9es \u00e0 la vie quotidienne. Ceci \u00e0 travers plusieurs questions et th\u00e9matiques qui se rejoignent : les institutions politiques, la participation citoyenne, la g\u00e9opolitique, la transition \u00e9nerg\u00e9tique et la justice climatique. Des ol\u00e9oducs et gazoducs au chauffage domestique, des \u00e9oliennes aux centres de recyclage, les infrastructures sont au c\u0153ur des d\u00e9bats actuels sur le changement syst\u00e9mique. Objets d'intenses contestations politiques, sociales et \u00e9conomiques, ces infrastructures divisent le pouvoir dans les deux sens du terme POWER : en tant qu'\u00e9nergie et en tant que politique.\n\nAujourd'hui, les architectes, les paysagistes, les artistes et les urbanistes sont encore souvent impliqu\u00e9s dans la perp\u00e9tuation du r\u00e9gime actuel de la modernit\u00e9 carbon\u00e9e. Pourtant, ils sont aussi dans une position cl\u00e9 pour faire \u00e9voluer le discours et la pratique vers une transition \u00e9nerg\u00e9tique \u00e0 grande \u00e9chelle.\n\nPOWER associera des r\u00e9f\u00e9rences historiques, des pratiques contemporaines et des projections vers l'avenir. Transdisciplinaire, elle pr\u00e9sentera les contributions d\u2019architectes, de paysagistes, d\u2019artistes, de philosophes, d\u2019historiens, de scientifiques, de l\u00e9gislateurs et d\u2019organisations non gouvernementales : Monira Al Qadiri, Rachel Armstrong, Sammy Baloji \/ Jean Katambayi \/ Daddy Tshikaya (On-Trade-Off), BAUKUNST, BC Architects \/ Babinigeysen \/ Schenk Hattori, Bernd and Hilla Becher, Oana Bogdan and Antoine Crahay, Constantin Brodzki, City Mine(d), Paul Duvigneaud, Feddes Olthof, Buckminster Fuller, Bruno Latour, Armin Linke, Andr\u00e9 and Jean Polak, Ren\u00e9 P\u00e9ch\u00e8re, Cedric Price, OMA\/AMO, Philippe Rahm, S+ \/ Arno Brandlhuber \/ Fosbury Architects, Fran\u00e7ois and Luc Schuiten, Karl Schwanzer, Bas Smets, Territorial Agency, The New Open \/ TU Delft, Willy Van Der Meeren, and Liam Young.\n\nParall\u00e8lement \u00e0 l'exposition, POWER comprend un programme public intense de conf\u00e9rences, tables rondes et projections auxquels participent notamment Thomas Auer, Daniel Barber, BC Architects, Oana Bogdan, Arno Brandlhuber, Koenraad Danneels, Andr\u00e9s Jaque, Jeanette Kuo, Charlotte Malterre-Barthes, Philippe Rahm, Bas Smets, Paulo Tavares, Ola Uduku et bien d'autres.\n\nDes workshops interg\u00e9n\u00e9rationnels seront \u00e9galement organis\u00e9s dans le cadre de l'exposition POWER en collaboration avec BC, V+, City Mine(d), Bento, Auranne Leray, Louise Lainiez et bien d'autres.\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"sp":{"name":"POWER SAVE THE DATE","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"},"nl":{"name":"POWER","shortdescr":"POWER legt de link tussen energie en beleid. De tentoonstelling en het bijbehorende programma nodigen uit na te denken over hoe de hedendaagse energie-infrastructuur zich verhoudt tot het dagelijks leven. Dit aan de hand van een aantal thema's die nauw met elkaar verbonden zijn: politieke instellingen, burgerparticipatie, geopolitiek, energietransitie en klimaatrechtvaardigheid","longdescr":"POWER legt de link tussen energie en beleid. De tentoonstelling en het bijbehorende programma nodigen uit na te denken over hoe de hedendaagse energie-infrastructuur zich verhoudt tot het dagelijks leven. Dit aan de hand van een aantal thema's die nauw met elkaar verbonden zijn: politieke instellingen, burgerparticipatie, geopolitiek, energietransitie en klimaatrechtvaardigheid. Van olie- en gaspijpleidingen tot de verwarming in huis, van windturbines tot recyclingcentra, infrastructuren leiden het debat rond de systemische verandering waar we vandaag getuige van zijn. Als voorwerpen van intense politieke, sociale en economische strijd verdelen deze systemen vermogen in beide betekenissen van het woord POWER : als energie en als beleid. \n\nVandaag de dag zijn architecten, landschapsontwerpers, kunstenaars en stedenbouwkundigen nog steeds verstrikt in de instandhouding van het huidige regime van de koolstofmoderniteit. Toch bevinden zij zich tegelijkertijd in een unieke positie om bij te dragen aan een evolutie in de richting van een energetische transformatie die grote politieke en maatschappelijke implicaties zou kunnen teweegbrengen.\n\nPOWER is een tentoonstelling die historische referenties, hedendaagse praktijken en speculaties over de toekomst samenbrengt. Met de participatie van een transdisciplinair veld van architecten, landschapsontwerpers, kunstenaars, filosofen, historici, wetenschappers, wetgevers en NGO's: Monira Al Qadiri, Rachel Armstrong, Sammy Baloji & Jean Katambayi & Daddy Tshikaya (On Trade Off), Arno Brandlhuber ETH Z\u00fcrich \/ B+ , BAUKUNST, BC Architects & Babinigeysen & Schenk Hattori, Bernd & Hilla Becher, Oana Bogdan, Citymine(d), Paul Duvigneaud, Buckminster Fuller, Armin Linke, Andr\u00e9 & Jean Polak, Ren\u00e9 P\u00e9ch\u00e8re, OMA\/AMO, Philippe Rahm, Bas Smets, Territorial Agency, TU Delft, Willy Van der Meeren, Liam Young, en vele anderen.\n\nParallel aan de tentoonstelling omvat het project POWER een uitgebreid publiek programma van lezingen, ronde tafelgesprekken en filmvertoningen met Thomas Auer, Daniel Barber, BC Architects, Oana Bogdan, Arno Brandlhuber, Koenraad Danneels, Andr\u00e9s Jaque, Jeanette Kuo, Charlotte Malterre-Barthes, Philippe Rahm, Bas Smets, Paulo Tavares, Ola Uduku and many more.\n\nIn het kader van de tentoonstelling POWER zullen ook intergenerationele workshops georganiseerd worden, in samenwerking met: BC, V+, City Mine(d), Bento, Auranne Leray, Louise Lainiez.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/civa.brussels\/fr\/expos-events\/power","email":"info@civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 642 24 50","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001752"}},"place":{"id":235577,"translations":{"de":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Das Architekturzentrum CIVA, das 2016 auf Betreiben der Region Br\u00fcssel-Hauptstadt ins Leben gerufen wurde, vereint in einer einzigen Struktur Ressourcen, Wissen und Know-how verschiedener Br\u00fcsseler Vereine aus dem Bereich Kultur, Architektur, St\u00e4dteplanung, Landschaftsarchitektur und Forschungen zum \u00d6kosystem: die Archive f\u00fcr moderne Architektur, die Bibliothek Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re, der Architekturfonds und das Centre Paul Duvigneaud.\r\nMit ihrem kulturellen Projekt tr\u00e4gt die Fondation CIA zur Entwicklung einer architektonischen, landschaftsarchitektonischen und st\u00e4dteplanerischen Kultur bei, die sich mit den Herausforderungen der Gegenwart auseinandersetzt. Schwerpunkt ist Br\u00fcssel. \r\n\r\nDie Fondation CIVA bietet eine ganze Reihe von Aktivit\u00e4ten und Angeboten: Ausstellungen, Konferenzen, Orte des Austauschs und der Debatten, p\u00e4dagogische Aktivit\u00e4ten, Archiveinblicke und Bibliotheken mit knapp 40.000 Werken und Zeitschriften zu den Themen Architektur, St\u00e4dteplanung, Stadtgeschichte, Landschaften, G\u00e4rten und urbane \u00d6kosysteme.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"CIVA is a museum, an archive center, a library and a meeting place for lovers of architecture, landscape architecture, urban ecosystems and history in Brussels. Throughout the year, CIVA organizes temporary exhibitions, lectures, debates, guided tours, book launches and activities for children. The activities are organized in Ixelles, near Place Flagey and in the center of Brussels, in KANAL - Centre Pompidou.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"CIVA","virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"CIVA est un muse\u0301e, un centre d'archives, une bibliothe\u0300que et un lieu de rencontre pour les amateurs d'architecture, d'architecture paysage\u0300re, d'e\u0301cosyste\u0300mes urbains et d'histoire a\u0300 Bruxelles. Tout au long de l'anne\u0301e, vous pouvez vous y rendre pour des expositions temporaires, des confe\u0301rences, des de\u0301bats, des visites guide\u0301es, des lancements de livres et des activite\u0301s pour les enfants. Les activite\u0301s se trouvent a\u0300 Ixelles, pre\u0300s de la Place Flagey et au centre de Bruxelles, a\u0300 KANAL - Centre Pompidou.\r\n\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"CIVA","virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Creado en 2016 por iniciativa de la Regi\u00f3n Bruselas-Capital, el CIVA re\u00fane una \u00fanica estructura de recursos, conocimiento y aprendizaje de varias asociaciones culturales activas en Bruselas en los campos de la arquitectura, urbanismo, paisajes y el estudio de ecosistemas: los Archivos de Arquitectura Moderna, la Biblioteca Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re, los Fondos para la arquitectura, el Centro Paul Duvigneaud y el CIVA asbl, ahora disuelto.\r\nA trav\u00e9s de este proyecto cultural, la Fundaci\u00f3n CIVA contribuye al desarrollo del paisaje arquitect\u00f3nico y la cultura urbana como base para afrontar desaf\u00edos contempor\u00e1neos, poniendo especial \u00e9nfasis en Bruselas.\r\nSiempre tiene \u00e9xito a la hora de cumplir sus objetivos y tratar con un p\u00fablico amplio (adultos y ni\u00f1os, estudiantes, investigadores, arquitectos, paisajistas, amantes de la naturaleza, pol\u00edticos, etc), la fundaci\u00f3n CIVA organiza numerosos eventos y actividades en diferentes lugares, incluyendo exhibiciones permanentes y temporales, conferencias, debates y actividades educativas. Tambi\u00e9n dispone archivos excepcionales abiertos para todos los p\u00fablicos (documentos de arquitectos y paisajistas: planos, bocetos, modelos, muebles, etc.) y librer\u00edas que contienen casi 40.000 obras y peri\u00f3dicos de arquitectura, urbanismo, la historia de los pueblos y ciudades, paisajes, jardines y ecolog\u00eda urbana.\r\nEstas actividades y materiales est\u00e1n dise\u00f1ados para despertar la curiosidad y el inter\u00e9s de todo nuestro entorno, ya sea un hecho hist\u00f3rico o una construcci\u00f3n.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Kluisstraat","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Kluisstraat","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"CIVA is een museum, een archiefcentrum, een bibliotheek en een ontmoetingsplek voor liefhebbers van architectuur, landschapsarchitectuur, stadsecosystemen en geschiedenis in Brussel. Het hele jaar door kan je er terecht voor tijdelijke tentoonstellingen, lezingen, debatten, rondleidingen, book launches en kinderactiviteiten. De activiteiten vind je in Elsene, vlakbij het Flageyplein en in Brussel-centrum, in KANAL \u2013 Centre Pompidou.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"CIVA","virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[5],"translations":{"de":["Flagey"],"pt":[null],"en":["Flagey"],"it":["Flagey"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Flagey"],"sp":["Flagey"],"nl":["Flagey"]}},"zones":{"list":[21],"translations":{"de":["S\u00fcden"],"pt":[null],"en":["South"],"it":["Sud"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Sud"],"sp":["Sur"],"nl":["Zuid"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":1436,"location":{"lat":50.82873218,"lon":4.36569034},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-01-25T14:25:12+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:14:20+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":235577,"translations":{"de":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Das Architekturzentrum CIVA, das 2016 auf Betreiben der Region Br\u00fcssel-Hauptstadt ins Leben gerufen wurde, vereint in einer einzigen Struktur Ressourcen, Wissen und Know-how verschiedener Br\u00fcsseler Vereine aus dem Bereich Kultur, Architektur, St\u00e4dteplanung, Landschaftsarchitektur und Forschungen zum \u00d6kosystem: die Archive f\u00fcr moderne Architektur, die Bibliothek Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re, der Architekturfonds und das Centre Paul Duvigneaud.\r\nMit ihrem kulturellen Projekt tr\u00e4gt die Fondation CIA zur Entwicklung einer architektonischen, landschaftsarchitektonischen und st\u00e4dteplanerischen Kultur bei, die sich mit den Herausforderungen der Gegenwart auseinandersetzt. Schwerpunkt ist Br\u00fcssel. \r\n\r\nDie Fondation CIVA bietet eine ganze Reihe von Aktivit\u00e4ten und Angeboten: Ausstellungen, Konferenzen, Orte des Austauschs und der Debatten, p\u00e4dagogische Aktivit\u00e4ten, Archiveinblicke und Bibliotheken mit knapp 40.000 Werken und Zeitschriften zu den Themen Architektur, St\u00e4dteplanung, Stadtgeschichte, Landschaften, G\u00e4rten und urbane \u00d6kosysteme.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"CIVA is a museum, an archive center, a library and a meeting place for lovers of architecture, landscape architecture, urban ecosystems and history in Brussels. Throughout the year, CIVA organizes temporary exhibitions, lectures, debates, guided tours, book launches and activities for children. The activities are organized in Ixelles, near Place Flagey and in the center of Brussels, in KANAL - Centre Pompidou.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"CIVA","virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"CIVA est un muse\u0301e, un centre d'archives, une bibliothe\u0300que et un lieu de rencontre pour les amateurs d'architecture, d'architecture paysage\u0300re, d'e\u0301cosyste\u0300mes urbains et d'histoire a\u0300 Bruxelles. Tout au long de l'anne\u0301e, vous pouvez vous y rendre pour des expositions temporaires, des confe\u0301rences, des de\u0301bats, des visites guide\u0301es, des lancements de livres et des activite\u0301s pour les enfants. Les activite\u0301s se trouvent a\u0300 Ixelles, pre\u0300s de la Place Flagey et au centre de Bruxelles, a\u0300 KANAL - Centre Pompidou.\r\n\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"CIVA","virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Creado en 2016 por iniciativa de la Regi\u00f3n Bruselas-Capital, el CIVA re\u00fane una \u00fanica estructura de recursos, conocimiento y aprendizaje de varias asociaciones culturales activas en Bruselas en los campos de la arquitectura, urbanismo, paisajes y el estudio de ecosistemas: los Archivos de Arquitectura Moderna, la Biblioteca Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re, los Fondos para la arquitectura, el Centro Paul Duvigneaud y el CIVA asbl, ahora disuelto.\r\nA trav\u00e9s de este proyecto cultural, la Fundaci\u00f3n CIVA contribuye al desarrollo del paisaje arquitect\u00f3nico y la cultura urbana como base para afrontar desaf\u00edos contempor\u00e1neos, poniendo especial \u00e9nfasis en Bruselas.\r\nSiempre tiene \u00e9xito a la hora de cumplir sus objetivos y tratar con un p\u00fablico amplio (adultos y ni\u00f1os, estudiantes, investigadores, arquitectos, paisajistas, amantes de la naturaleza, pol\u00edticos, etc), la fundaci\u00f3n CIVA organiza numerosos eventos y actividades en diferentes lugares, incluyendo exhibiciones permanentes y temporales, conferencias, debates y actividades educativas. Tambi\u00e9n dispone archivos excepcionales abiertos para todos los p\u00fablicos (documentos de arquitectos y paisajistas: planos, bocetos, modelos, muebles, etc.) y librer\u00edas que contienen casi 40.000 obras y peri\u00f3dicos de arquitectura, urbanismo, la historia de los pueblos y ciudades, paisajes, jardines y ecolog\u00eda urbana.\r\nEstas actividades y materiales est\u00e1n dise\u00f1ados para despertar la curiosidad y el inter\u00e9s de todo nuestro entorno, ya sea un hecho hist\u00f3rico o una construcci\u00f3n.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Kluisstraat","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+ 32 (0)2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Kluisstraat","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"CIVA is een museum, een archiefcentrum, een bibliotheek en een ontmoetingsplek voor liefhebbers van architectuur, landschapsarchitectuur, stadsecosystemen en geschiedenis in Brussel. Het hele jaar door kan je er terecht voor tijdelijke tentoonstellingen, lezingen, debatten, rondleidingen, book launches en kinderactiviteiten. De activiteiten vind je in Elsene, vlakbij het Flageyplein en in Brussel-centrum, in KANAL \u2013 Centre Pompidou.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"CIVA","virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":1436,"location":{"lat":50.82873218,"lon":4.36569034},"last_updated_at":"2024-01-25T14:25:12+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:14:20+02:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/79e69311522303076334e2732c3f663712a274f1.jpg","width":1160,"height":708,"ratio":1,"oEmbed_height":708,"oEmbed_width":1160,"translations":{"de":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"pt":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"en":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"it":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"cn":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"fr":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"sp":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe Rahm"},"nl":{"title":"Climatic Apparel\/About A Worker, 2020.","copyright":"Philippe R